-%   one-shot interceptors (see |\caption@client@before|): one for the |\stepcounter|
-%   of the float counter (so we can decide if the counter will be stepped, which depends
-%   on |\ContinuedFloat| and on sub-captions placed above), and one for the |\@dblarg|
-%   which follows the counter step (so we know whether |\caption*| was used,
-%   and can process the arguments with |\caption@dblarg|).
-% \item Our plug \texttt{caption} for \texttt{caption/listentry} prepares the
